00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:04,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:02,310 --> 00:00:03,900
[Death Confirmation Report]
Now that Cheung Wai Keung is dead,

2
00:00:03,920 --> 00:00:05,260
I've got a new assignment for you.

3
00:00:05,280 --> 00:00:06,290
Thank you, sir!

4
00:00:07,040 --> 00:00:08,210
You're here to poach him already?

5
00:00:08,230 --> 00:00:08,980
Aren't you a bit too eager?

6
00:00:09,000 --> 00:00:11,370
I heard the force's rising star is finally available,

7
00:00:11,390 --> 00:00:12,930
so of course I came straight over to poach him.

8
00:00:12,950 --> 00:00:13,690
This is Mok Fei Foon.

9
00:00:13,920 --> 00:00:15,420
He's joining the CCB today.
[*CCB: Commercial Crime Bureau]

10
00:00:15,630 --> 00:00:17,050
According to information from Interpol,

11
00:00:17,520 --> 00:00:19,980
a transnational counterfeiting syndicate called "Dreamweaver"

12
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:21,580
may have arrived

13
00:00:21,600 --> 00:00:23,180
in Hong Kong, China over the past year.

14
00:00:23,200 --> 00:00:25,340
There are two major sources of counterfeit money in Hong Kong, China.

15
00:00:25,520 --> 00:00:27,100
One is the long-established syndicate, Eastern Hall.

16
00:00:27,120 --> 00:00:29,180
[Ho Tung Fong]
In a previous deal, the other side

17
00:00:29,200 --> 00:00:30,500
caught them paying in counterfeit notes.

18
00:00:30,630 --> 00:00:31,450
The second

19
00:00:31,470 --> 00:00:32,420
is Sheng Tung's uncle,

20
00:00:32,630 --> 00:00:33,500
To Si Hong.

21
00:00:34,920 --> 00:00:35,930
Don't play games with me.

22
00:00:35,950 --> 00:00:37,130
Where did you get those counterfeit notes?

23
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:41,260
You said your counterfeit notes were top-notch.

24
00:00:41,520 --> 00:00:42,740
How did anyone know they were fake?

25
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:44,050
No matter how good the quality is,

26
00:00:44,230 --> 00:00:45,130
they're still counterfeit.

27
00:00:45,280 --> 00:00:46,450
Use too many at once,

28
00:00:46,470 --> 00:00:47,340
and it's bound to raise suspicion.

29
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:48,530
Look at my hand.

30
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:50,050
I lost a finger!

31
00:00:50,630 --> 00:00:51,610
I'm warning you,

32
00:00:51,630 --> 00:00:52,530
crossing Sheng Tung...

33
00:01:26,880 --> 00:01:29,620
♪With you, it's like I can breathe again♪

34
00:01:30,050 --> 00:01:32,820
♪I can't live without this breath, this heartbeat♪

35
00:01:32,940 --> 00:01:35,730
♪Forever's too far, but you're right here♪

36
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:38,160
♪Together we'll take on this jaded world♪

37
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:41,140
♪With you, I'll cross the dark, outrun the pain, and run away♪

38
00:01:41,220 --> 00:01:45,300
♪Still believing in true love, no matter how naive, calling you♪

39
00:01:46,880 --> 00:01:50,090
♪I'm willing to wait♪

40
00:01:50,940 --> 00:01:53,780
♪I love you like you're a part of me♪

41
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:56,580
♪I want to share my life with you♪

42
00:01:57,220 --> 00:02:03,000
♪To love this deeply, I'll give a little more♪

43
00:02:03,350 --> 00:02:05,150
♪In this cold and gray city♪

44
00:02:05,230 --> 00:02:06,860
♪Through all the pain, I'll hold you. Is it true?♪

45
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:09,310
♪Pieces of our memories slowly fade♪

46
00:02:09,390 --> 00:02:09,970
♪Stay with me♪

47
00:02:10,110 --> 00:02:12,720
♪Do you remember the day we crossed paths?♪

48
00:02:12,800 --> 00:02:13,500
♪Stay with me♪

49
00:02:13,580 --> 00:02:16,420
♪Do you remember the forever we promised?♪

50
00:02:16,910 --> 00:02:18,920
♪Who's waiting for you to save them?♪

51
00:02:19,450 --> 00:02:21,960
♪My heart aches, breaks, and struggles on♪

52
00:02:22,490 --> 00:02:25,000
♪How can I hold on to everything in one moment?♪

53
00:02:25,720 --> 00:02:29,220
♪Stop blaming fate and learn to let it be♪

54
00:02:31,070 --> 00:02:33,100
[Ash]
[Episode 3]

55
00:02:42,470 --> 00:02:43,690
Hey! Cut it out!

56
00:02:45,070 --> 00:02:46,450
Are you crazy?

57
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:53,020
What are you up to now?

58
00:02:55,040 --> 00:02:55,820
I'll help you get undressed.

59
00:02:57,310 --> 00:02:58,900
If you keep this up,

60
00:02:59,070 --> 00:03:00,900
I'll report you for trespassing.

61
00:03:01,120 --> 00:03:01,900
Come on.

62
00:03:07,360 --> 00:03:08,130
Take it off.

63
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:12,530
Sit.

64
00:03:18,000 --> 00:03:19,530
Sit. I'll wash your hair.

65
00:03:27,470 --> 00:03:28,610
To,

66
00:03:28,920 --> 00:03:30,850
you actually know what you're doing.

67
00:03:34,470 --> 00:03:36,130
When my brother was little,

68
00:03:36,680 --> 00:03:38,900
I was always the one who bathed him.

69
00:03:49,150 --> 00:03:50,050
It's healed.

70
00:03:51,310 --> 00:03:52,050
What?

71
00:03:56,710 --> 00:03:57,500
Oh, this?

72
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,580
Yeah, got hit by an ashtray.

73
00:04:02,870 --> 00:04:04,180
It's nothing.

74
00:04:04,550 --> 00:04:06,180
My hair usually covers it.

75
00:04:06,200 --> 00:04:06,930
People can't tell.

76
00:04:10,390 --> 00:04:11,210
I'm sorry.

77
00:04:15,200 --> 00:04:16,660
Why are you making that face?

78
00:04:18,070 --> 00:04:20,530
I won't let anything like that happen again.

79
00:04:45,150 --> 00:04:46,770
Don't touch the wound.

80
00:04:47,200 --> 00:04:48,260
I know.

81
00:04:56,950 --> 00:04:58,660
You're blowing germs into the wound.

82
00:05:01,390 --> 00:05:02,820
Then I'll disinfect it again, okay?

83
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:04,340
Keep it up, and you'll regret it.

84
00:05:27,470 --> 00:05:28,260
All done.

85
00:05:30,200 --> 00:05:33,260
If you're done, I'm going to rest.

86
00:05:35,360 --> 00:05:36,260
Get up.

87
00:05:36,870 --> 00:05:38,050
Your hair's still wet.

88
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:40,450
It's okay.

89
00:05:41,310 --> 00:05:42,050
No, it's not.

90
00:05:42,070 --> 00:05:43,420
You'll get a headache and catch a chill.

91
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:55,100
Are you still with the Narcotics Bureau?

92
00:05:56,470 --> 00:05:57,900
I've been transferred to the CCB.

93
00:05:59,150 --> 00:06:00,290
Why ask all of a sudden?

94
00:06:01,710 --> 00:06:04,450
Shouldn't it be much safer

95
00:06:04,550 --> 00:06:06,450
in the Commercial Crime Bureau?

96
00:06:06,630 --> 00:06:08,180
How did you get hurt?

97
00:06:09,600 --> 00:06:11,660
I was attacked by someone with a knife.

98
00:06:11,680 --> 00:06:13,690
I fell dodging him and scraped myself.

99
00:06:13,710 --> 00:06:14,850
It's only a minor injury.

100
00:06:16,680 --> 00:06:17,450
Someone with a knife?

101
00:06:18,360 --> 00:06:19,370
What do you mean?

102
00:06:19,920 --> 00:06:20,900
Were you in danger?

103
00:06:22,470 --> 00:06:23,660
Calm down.

104
00:06:23,680 --> 00:06:24,820
We're tracking him down.

105
00:06:25,230 --> 00:06:26,820
We'll find him soon.

106
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:28,740
How do you expect me to calm down?

107
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:31,900
Am I supposed to wait until something happens to you and then regret it?

108
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:36,580
Why do you suddenly care so much about me?

109
00:06:39,950 --> 00:06:41,820
You don't know how to look after yourself.

110
00:06:42,520 --> 00:06:43,770
Find another job.

111
00:06:44,230 --> 00:06:45,180
Find another job?

112
00:06:45,310 --> 00:06:46,180
What job?

113
00:06:46,550 --> 00:06:47,820
Anything.

114
00:06:47,840 --> 00:06:49,370
Just stop being a police officer.

115
00:06:50,200 --> 00:06:53,050
You can be head of security at my company.

116
00:06:53,680 --> 00:06:54,930
Or you can

117
00:06:54,950 --> 00:06:55,820
just retire.

118
00:06:57,040 --> 00:06:57,770
Retire?

119
00:06:58,280 --> 00:06:59,420
Are you going to support me?

120
00:06:59,630 --> 00:07:00,500
Sure.

121
00:07:00,710 --> 00:07:01,820
I can afford it.

122
00:07:02,390 --> 00:07:03,180
Right.

123
00:07:03,280 --> 00:07:04,420
I almost forgot.

124
00:07:04,440 --> 00:07:06,130
You're the business world's most eligible bachelor.

125
00:07:07,790 --> 00:07:09,340
I'm just a regular cop.

126
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:11,660
I wouldn't cost you much.

127
00:07:13,710 --> 00:07:15,290
Then I'll take that as a yes.

128
00:07:15,390 --> 00:07:18,420
Hand in your resignation first thing tomorrow.

129
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:19,420
You're ridiculous.

130
00:07:19,440 --> 00:07:20,450
Who said I agreed?

131
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:32,500
How about this?

132
00:07:34,280 --> 00:07:35,850
I made you mad before,

133
00:07:36,230 --> 00:07:37,450
and now you've made me mad.

134
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:39,610
Let's call it even, okay?

135
00:07:40,200 --> 00:07:41,900
No more fighting from now on, okay?

136
00:07:59,280 --> 00:08:00,420
Lucky you.

137
00:08:01,040 --> 00:08:02,660
I'm generous enough to let it slide.

138
00:08:03,390 --> 00:08:05,020
You don't get many chances like this.

139
00:08:06,310 --> 00:08:08,290
So behave yourself from now on. Got it?

140
00:08:08,520 --> 00:08:09,930
Same goes for you.

141
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:11,260
Me? What about me?

142
00:08:12,470 --> 00:08:14,290
I'm the only one you can have.

143
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,130
I'll think about it.

144
00:08:24,470 --> 00:08:25,370
Where are you going?

145
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:26,980
To get the hairdryer.

146
00:08:28,840 --> 00:08:29,580
Why?

147
00:08:29,710 --> 00:08:30,770
Do you want me to stay?

148
00:08:31,790 --> 00:08:32,580
Yes.

149
00:08:51,950 --> 00:08:52,820
Forget it.

150
00:08:54,280 --> 00:08:55,370
So we'll just sleep?

151
00:09:01,760 --> 00:09:02,500
Okay.

152
00:11:54,280 --> 00:11:55,050
Morning.

153
00:11:55,950 --> 00:11:56,740
You're up?

154
00:11:57,790 --> 00:11:58,660
What are you making?

155
00:11:59,920 --> 00:12:02,580
An all-day breakfast just for you.

156
00:12:02,920 --> 00:12:05,770
Sausages, toast and fried eggs.

157
00:12:06,710 --> 00:12:09,450
And I just went out for cherry tomatoes and lettuce.

158
00:12:12,470 --> 00:12:14,820
So you just cook everything in the pan,

159
00:12:14,840 --> 00:12:18,100
then take it out and plate it up?

160
00:12:18,360 --> 00:12:19,690
Are you eating it or not?

161
00:12:19,950 --> 00:12:21,770
Of course.

162
00:12:22,950 --> 00:12:24,660
I'll eat anything you make.

163
00:12:26,600 --> 00:12:29,500
It's just that the sesame dressing has expired.

164
00:12:29,840 --> 00:12:30,690
Do you mind?

165
00:12:31,390 --> 00:12:32,130
Let me see.

166
00:12:34,070 --> 00:12:35,980
It's fine as long as it hasn't gone bad.

167
00:12:39,390 --> 00:12:40,370
Does your wound still hurt?

168
00:12:43,310 --> 00:12:44,180
It's okay.

169
00:12:44,200 --> 00:12:45,370
Still hurts a little.

170
00:12:50,710 --> 00:12:51,500
Let me do it.

171
00:12:51,630 --> 00:12:53,020
No. You'll ruin it.

172
00:12:54,870 --> 00:12:56,100
Are you hungry?

173
00:12:57,150 --> 00:12:58,770
Have some fruit first.

174
00:13:20,870 --> 00:13:22,740
What time are you going back to the station today?

175
00:13:23,520 --> 00:13:26,850
My boss wants me checked for any bone injuries.

176
00:13:26,870 --> 00:13:28,450
I've got an appointment this afternoon.

177
00:13:28,870 --> 00:13:31,900
So we can do whatever you want till then.

178
00:13:34,280 --> 00:13:35,100
Whatever I want?

179
00:13:35,440 --> 00:13:36,210
Mm-hmm.

180
00:14:14,440 --> 00:14:15,290
Come here.

181
00:14:17,760 --> 00:14:18,610
What are you up to?

182
00:14:23,150 --> 00:14:24,020
What do you think?

183
00:14:59,630 --> 00:15:00,420
Oh...

184
00:15:02,070 --> 00:15:04,020
All that effort, wasted.

185
00:15:04,390 --> 00:15:05,420
It's all your fault.

186
00:15:05,710 --> 00:15:08,420
All you think about is making out.

187
00:15:17,950 --> 00:15:19,210
It's burnt, and you're still eating it?

188
00:15:19,760 --> 00:15:21,340
It could give you cancer.

189
00:15:23,950 --> 00:15:25,370
Well, you made it.

190
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,210
I told you.

191
00:15:39,230 --> 00:15:40,530
Your assistant's calling.

192
00:15:40,760 --> 00:15:41,660
Hello?

193
00:15:41,950 --> 00:15:42,900
Where are you now?

194
00:15:43,070 --> 00:15:44,340
Do you have other meetings today?

195
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:47,770
Hello, it's me.

196
00:15:48,710 --> 00:15:50,370
Who was that?

197
00:15:54,070 --> 00:15:55,020
What do you need?

198
00:15:55,630 --> 00:15:57,530
You have a meeting with a government department later.

199
00:15:58,310 --> 00:15:59,740
You should get going soon.

200
00:16:00,680 --> 00:16:01,500
Where are you now?

201
00:16:02,070 --> 00:16:03,100
I'm...

202
00:16:03,120 --> 00:16:03,900
In Yuen Long.

203
00:16:07,840 --> 00:16:10,370
Okay. Please make yourself presentable before you head out.

204
00:16:10,390 --> 00:16:12,420
I'll send you the address after I hang up.

205
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:18,290
Did you do that on purpose?

206
00:16:18,680 --> 00:16:19,450
What?

207
00:16:20,230 --> 00:16:21,340
Can't I tease you?

208
00:16:22,470 --> 00:16:24,370
Hey, stop.

209
00:16:26,380 --> 00:16:28,460
[Sham Shuh Po Police Station]

210
00:16:40,150 --> 00:16:40,930
Officer Mok,

211
00:16:41,280 --> 00:16:43,020
what's got you so happy?

212
00:16:44,390 --> 00:16:45,450
Mind your own business.

213
00:16:46,120 --> 00:16:48,210
Any leads on that motorbike I asked you to check?

214
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:49,450
I checked.

215
00:16:49,760 --> 00:16:50,690
The number plate was fake.

216
00:16:50,920 --> 00:16:52,690
None of the CCTV cameras on the nearby streets

217
00:16:52,710 --> 00:16:53,820
caught him.

218
00:16:55,040 --> 00:16:56,020
But I have a theory.

219
00:16:57,230 --> 00:16:58,100
Look at you, taking initiative.

220
00:16:58,120 --> 00:16:59,050
Let's hear it.

221
00:17:00,390 --> 00:17:03,130
I think the casino owner was trying to have us killed.

222
00:17:04,710 --> 00:17:05,420
Go on.

223
00:17:05,920 --> 00:17:06,660
Think about it.

224
00:17:07,000 --> 00:17:08,980
If the casino owner hadn't wanted us dead

225
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:10,130
to keep his secret,

226
00:17:10,280 --> 00:17:13,450
why would someone on a motorbike have attacked us with a knife

227
00:17:13,630 --> 00:17:15,660
right when To Si Hong was leaving the casino?

228
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:17,580
They must've known we were tailing him.

229
00:17:17,950 --> 00:17:20,130
As soon as we started investigating the casino, they made their move.

230
00:17:20,440 --> 00:17:23,610
They must've been afraid we'd uncover their link to the counterfeit money case.

231
00:17:24,150 --> 00:17:25,020
I don't think so.

232
00:17:25,280 --> 00:17:26,050
Why not?

233
00:17:27,120 --> 00:17:27,900
Think it through.

234
00:17:30,040 --> 00:17:33,340
If the casino owner had wanted to protect To Si Hong,

235
00:17:33,470 --> 00:17:35,850
he wouldn't have let To Si Hong show his face before making a move.

236
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:38,530
And he definitely wouldn't have launched an attack on his own turf.

237
00:17:38,760 --> 00:17:40,180
That would've been asking to get caught.

238
00:17:40,470 --> 00:17:41,770
That's not how they operate.

239
00:17:43,230 --> 00:17:45,290
Maybe they were just trying to scare us off the investigation.

240
00:17:45,550 --> 00:17:48,050
But that man came straight at us with a knife.

241
00:17:48,150 --> 00:17:49,740
He attacked without hesitation.

242
00:17:49,760 --> 00:17:51,100
He was out to kill us.

243
00:17:51,710 --> 00:17:52,580
So I don't think

244
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:55,020
it was just someone the casino owner hired to scare us.

245
00:17:55,470 --> 00:17:56,260
Really?

246
00:17:57,440 --> 00:17:59,610
I've got more experience with cases like this than you.

247
00:17:59,630 --> 00:18:00,580
Trust me.

248
00:18:01,470 --> 00:18:03,850
But we got attacked as soon as we started investigating the casino.

249
00:18:03,870 --> 00:18:05,050
What are the odds?

250
00:18:05,120 --> 00:18:07,980
I still think the casino is involved.

251
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:08,820
Fair point.

252
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:11,580
But being involved doesn't mean they were behind the attack.

253
00:18:12,390 --> 00:18:14,370
Sir, that's too deep for me.

254
00:18:15,150 --> 00:18:16,210
By your logic,

255
00:18:16,230 --> 00:18:17,820
what leads do we have left to follow?

256
00:18:18,120 --> 00:18:18,980
Want to learn?

257
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:20,290
Make me tea and call me Master first.

258
00:18:20,310 --> 00:18:21,050
What?

259
00:18:25,920 --> 00:18:27,690
I was kidding. Come with me.

260
00:18:27,760 --> 00:18:28,580
Okay.

261
00:18:29,860 --> 00:18:32,860
[Tin Ping Group Sales Department]

262
00:18:33,120 --> 00:18:35,210
We still can't find Uncle To.

263
00:18:35,520 --> 00:18:37,420
I went to his home and office,

264
00:18:37,440 --> 00:18:38,740
but I found nothing.

265
00:18:39,390 --> 00:18:41,500
Do we know who Uncle To has been in contact with lately?

266
00:18:42,040 --> 00:18:43,130
I asked Auntie Fan.

267
00:18:43,150 --> 00:18:44,130
She hasn't seen

268
00:18:44,150 --> 00:18:46,500
anyone suspicious around him.

269
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:51,770
So nothing on anyone he might be working with?

270
00:18:54,790 --> 00:18:56,610
Luk King, stay out of this.

271
00:18:56,870 --> 00:18:58,850
Leave the investigation entirely to Tam Fung.

272
00:18:59,550 --> 00:19:01,260
Is your stomach acting up?

273
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:05,130
Do you need me to take you to hospital?

274
00:19:07,710 --> 00:19:09,290
No. There's no time.

275
00:19:16,920 --> 00:19:18,260
Feros has been

276
00:19:18,390 --> 00:19:19,820
competing with us for some time

277
00:19:20,150 --> 00:19:22,450
and has worked with others to take several projects from us.

278
00:19:22,790 --> 00:19:24,690
A lot of our business partners have gone over to them.

279
00:19:25,600 --> 00:19:27,850
To put it nicely, they're waiting to see how things play out.

280
00:19:28,360 --> 00:19:30,130
To put it harshly, they're waiting for us to lose.

281
00:19:33,520 --> 00:19:36,100
Make sure everything is properly arranged for the ceremony later.

282
00:19:36,310 --> 00:19:37,690
There can't be any mistakes.

283
00:19:39,200 --> 00:19:41,210
Loek To, don't worry too much.

284
00:19:41,710 --> 00:19:44,020
Feros only entered the Hong Kong, China market and went public last year,

285
00:19:44,120 --> 00:19:45,210
yet they've been poaching staff and snapping up projects,

286
00:19:45,230 --> 00:19:46,450
expanding with almost no regard for cost.

287
00:19:46,550 --> 00:19:48,450
I don't think they can keep it up for long.

288
00:19:49,150 --> 00:19:50,850
Even if they can't,

289
00:19:51,040 --> 00:19:52,020
I can't just sit back

290
00:19:52,040 --> 00:19:54,690
while they keep poaching our business partners.

291
00:19:56,150 --> 00:19:57,130
Luk King, you know,

292
00:19:58,120 --> 00:19:59,980
capital, time, and corporate reputation

293
00:20:00,280 --> 00:20:01,900
are all intangible costs to the company.

294
00:20:04,600 --> 00:20:06,580
I looked into their corporate background.

295
00:20:06,600 --> 00:20:08,500
Feros's parent company is in the UK

296
00:20:08,790 --> 00:20:10,820
and works closely with numerous overseas investors.

297
00:20:11,470 --> 00:20:12,660
Its CEO,

298
00:20:12,680 --> 00:20:14,420
who returned from the UK, is from Hong Kong, China.

299
00:20:15,120 --> 00:20:16,770
But I couldn't find much about him.

300
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:19,130
I remember his surname is Siu, though.

301
00:20:19,150 --> 00:20:20,100
Does that ring a bell?

302
00:20:20,150 --> 00:20:20,850
No.

303
00:20:21,790 --> 00:20:23,500
There are so many people out there.

304
00:20:23,710 --> 00:20:25,100
I can't possibly know them all.

305
00:20:27,520 --> 00:20:28,690
We should get going.

306
00:20:29,840 --> 00:20:30,610
Let's go.

307
00:20:30,710 --> 00:20:31,500
Okay.

308
00:20:38,500 --> 00:20:40,900
[Tin Ping Group and Ascend Global Estates Limited Signing Ceremony]

309
00:20:55,200 --> 00:20:57,210
Distinguished guests and members of the media,

310
00:20:57,230 --> 00:20:59,290
welcome to Bay Area Metropolis's

311
00:20:59,310 --> 00:21:01,450
phase one partnership signing ceremony.

312
00:21:01,550 --> 00:21:03,660
Bay Area Metropolis is a key development project

313
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:05,210
for Tin Ping Group.

314
00:21:05,470 --> 00:21:08,050
It is designed to create a new-generation urban hub in Hong Kong, China

315
00:21:08,070 --> 00:21:11,290
that brings together living, community, business, and leisure.

316
00:21:11,550 --> 00:21:13,130
We're delighted to announce

317
00:21:13,310 --> 00:21:15,450
that Ascend Global Estates Limited will be joining us

318
00:21:15,470 --> 00:21:17,290
as our phase one development partner.

319
00:21:17,310 --> 00:21:20,180
Now, let's welcome Chairman Yiu King Leung of Ascend Global Estates Limited

320
00:21:20,230 --> 00:21:22,690
and Chairman Hui Loek To of Tin Ping Group

321
00:21:22,840 --> 00:21:25,340
to complete this simple yet formal signing ceremony.

322
00:21:25,470 --> 00:21:26,340
Please welcome them.

323
00:21:35,460 --> 00:21:41,780
[Mr. Hui Loek To, Chairman of Tin Ping Group]

324
00:21:52,280 --> 00:21:53,500
No need to wait.

325
00:21:54,280 --> 00:21:55,820
Chairman Yiu won't be able to make it today.

326
00:21:57,920 --> 00:21:58,930
Hello, everyone.

327
00:21:59,630 --> 00:22:00,420
My surname is Siu.

328
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:02,770
I'm the CEO of Feros Group.

329
00:22:03,920 --> 00:22:05,020
You can call me Shawn.

330
00:22:05,870 --> 00:22:06,850
Feros Group

331
00:22:07,150 --> 00:22:08,900
has just completed its acquisition of Ascend Global Estates,

332
00:22:09,360 --> 00:22:11,290
so I'm attending today's event

333
00:22:12,920 --> 00:22:14,690
in my new capacity as CEO.

334
00:22:21,070 --> 00:22:22,500
You don't mind if I call you Shawn, do you?

335
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:23,980
Mr. Hui,

336
00:22:24,230 --> 00:22:26,290
you don't mind if I call you Vincent, do you?

337
00:22:27,790 --> 00:22:29,530
New management, new approach.

338
00:22:30,600 --> 00:22:32,210
You've been in Hong Kong, China for less than a year,

339
00:22:32,520 --> 00:22:35,500
yet every move you've made has taken everyone by surprise.

340
00:22:36,710 --> 00:22:38,260
I'll take that as a compliment, Vincent.

341
00:22:39,550 --> 00:22:40,690
I do admire

342
00:22:40,710 --> 00:22:42,660
the way you've run Tin Ping Group all these years.

343
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:44,690
I look forward to a chance to work together in the future.

344
00:22:45,150 --> 00:22:45,930
Just

345
00:22:46,760 --> 00:22:47,530
not on this project.

346
00:22:48,040 --> 00:22:50,210
You mean you're ending this partnership?

347
00:22:50,630 --> 00:22:51,420
That's right.

348
00:22:52,150 --> 00:22:54,180
We've reviewed Tin Ping's financial position.

349
00:22:54,520 --> 00:22:56,130
I doubt you can even handle

350
00:22:56,150 --> 00:22:57,580
a project as big as Bay Area Metropolis.

351
00:22:58,950 --> 00:23:00,930
I won't let Ascend get dragged down.

352
00:23:03,000 --> 00:23:03,930
That's fine.

353
00:23:04,550 --> 00:23:06,740
I rarely work with partners I don't know anyway,

354
00:23:07,360 --> 00:23:10,290
especially those who don't understand the local market

355
00:23:10,600 --> 00:23:12,100
yet invest blindly.

356
00:23:12,840 --> 00:23:14,740
Ending the partnership between Tin Ping and Ascend

357
00:23:17,150 --> 00:23:18,530
does us more good than harm.

358
00:23:19,120 --> 00:23:20,370
I completely agree.

359
00:23:21,390 --> 00:23:23,260
But frankly, Vincent,

360
00:23:23,710 --> 00:23:25,740
you'd better check Tin Ping's cash flow.

361
00:23:26,550 --> 00:23:27,740
If you find a shortfall

362
00:23:27,950 --> 00:23:30,210
and need to work with Feros,

363
00:23:30,950 --> 00:23:31,900
come talk to me anytime.

364
00:23:33,230 --> 00:23:34,100
Sure.

365
00:23:34,710 --> 00:23:35,980
I'm sure we'll get the chance.

366
00:23:36,200 --> 00:23:37,450
Now, if you'll excuse me.

367
00:23:38,660 --> 00:23:40,660
[Mr. Yiu King Leung]

368
00:23:41,390 --> 00:23:42,180
I have a feeling

369
00:23:44,230 --> 00:23:45,340
we'll be seeing each other again soon.

370
00:23:46,680 --> 00:23:47,450
I look forward to it.

371
00:24:01,000 --> 00:24:02,530
Officer Mok, where exactly are you taking me?

372
00:24:02,550 --> 00:24:03,610
To meet a real expert.

373
00:24:03,630 --> 00:24:04,530
He really knows his stuff.

374
00:24:05,120 --> 00:24:05,850
Who is it?

375
00:24:05,870 --> 00:24:06,900
Why so many questions?

376
00:24:06,950 --> 00:24:08,180
You'll find out soon enough.

377
00:24:08,280 --> 00:24:08,850
Right.

378
00:24:08,950 --> 00:24:09,690
Hey, Fung Gor.

379
00:24:14,040 --> 00:24:14,850
You scared me,

380
00:24:14,870 --> 00:24:15,820
Mok Fei Foon.

381
00:24:16,070 --> 00:24:16,820
Long time no see.

382
00:24:16,840 --> 00:24:17,660
I thought you were dead.

383
00:24:17,680 --> 00:24:18,770
Don't curse me.

384
00:24:18,790 --> 00:24:20,450
I was going to ask you out for a ride.

385
00:24:21,150 --> 00:24:22,370
You wouldn't come all this way for nothing.

386
00:24:22,550 --> 00:24:23,290
What do you want?

387
00:24:24,040 --> 00:24:25,740
I need to ask you something.

388
00:24:26,070 --> 00:24:27,850
Has any one of your customers brought in

389
00:24:27,870 --> 00:24:29,260
a motorbike for modification recently?

390
00:24:29,550 --> 00:24:32,260
A 2020 Yamaha R1.

391
00:24:32,280 --> 00:24:33,340
Slim build,

392
00:24:33,360 --> 00:24:34,930
about 1.75 metres tall.

393
00:24:35,920 --> 00:24:38,130
I get tons of customers here.

394
00:24:38,150 --> 00:24:39,690
How am I supposed to remember them all?

395
00:24:39,950 --> 00:24:41,500
Maybe you don't remember the person,

396
00:24:41,520 --> 00:24:42,770
but surely you remember the bike.

397
00:24:43,470 --> 00:24:45,020
Pretty much everyone in Hong Kong, China

398
00:24:45,040 --> 00:24:46,180
comes to you for motorbike modifications,

399
00:24:46,200 --> 00:24:47,050
right?

400
00:24:48,680 --> 00:24:49,930
Think carefully.

401
00:24:50,710 --> 00:24:54,290
The body and rims were both wrapped in gold and blue,

402
00:24:55,520 --> 00:24:58,930
with a ten-centimetre scratch above the left headlight.

403
00:24:59,760 --> 00:25:01,370
It came at us so fast,

404
00:25:01,390 --> 00:25:02,580
and you still saw all that?

405
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:04,850
Do I have to tell you I've got eagle eyes?

406
00:25:08,070 --> 00:25:08,850
I remember now.

407
00:25:08,870 --> 00:25:09,900
That guy said he'd

408
00:25:10,150 --> 00:25:12,050
just bought the bike and brought it in for modifications.

409
00:25:12,470 --> 00:25:14,500
But I could tell straight away it wasn't legit.

410
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:16,850
He paid me very well,

411
00:25:17,070 --> 00:25:18,260
so I didn't ask questions.

412
00:25:19,200 --> 00:25:22,020
Do you remember anything distinctive about his appearance?

413
00:25:23,150 --> 00:25:24,130
Distinctive?

414
00:25:25,440 --> 00:25:29,050
He had a lightning-bolt tattoo on the back of his neck.

415
00:25:30,470 --> 00:25:33,100
I also heard him refer to himself

416
00:25:35,120 --> 00:25:35,900
as K on the phone.

417
00:25:51,710 --> 00:25:52,690
Yee Gor, don't worry.

418
00:25:53,870 --> 00:25:55,260
I'll take care of him

419
00:25:56,120 --> 00:25:56,930
and avenge you.

420
00:26:01,520 --> 00:26:04,100
So the knifeman at the casino was after you.

421
00:26:04,120 --> 00:26:05,930
Officer Mok, what are you going to do?

422
00:26:06,310 --> 00:26:07,980
I'll report it to my superior.

423
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:09,100
Don't worry about it.

424
00:26:13,120 --> 00:26:15,740
[Hui Loek To: Are you done with work? Where should I pick you up?]

425
00:26:16,150 --> 00:26:16,690
All right.

426
00:26:16,710 --> 00:26:17,770
It's quitting time.

427
00:26:17,790 --> 00:26:18,690
Go home and get some rest.

428
00:26:19,230 --> 00:26:20,020
Sir,

429
00:26:20,550 --> 00:26:22,450
didn't you say we'd leave after finishing what we were working on?

430
00:26:22,550 --> 00:26:24,290
We just found a new lead.

431
00:26:25,070 --> 00:26:26,450
You want to work overtime?

432
00:26:26,840 --> 00:26:27,850
Perfect.

433
00:26:28,230 --> 00:26:29,900
Go check the stolen-vehicle records.

434
00:26:30,200 --> 00:26:31,660
You know how to do that, right?

435
00:26:33,070 --> 00:26:33,740
Bye-bye.

436
00:26:33,760 --> 00:26:34,210
But...

437
00:26:34,680 --> 00:26:35,530
Get to it.

438
00:26:35,550 --> 00:26:36,900
Don't hold me up. I'm meeting someone.

439
00:26:39,360 --> 00:26:40,130
Yes, sir.

440
00:26:41,180 --> 00:26:44,940
♪Let the world judge all it wants♪

441
00:26:44,940 --> 00:26:48,620
♪All I want is that when we meet, I can smile♪

442
00:26:48,620 --> 00:26:52,420
♪And say, "I'm so glad it's you"♪

443
00:26:52,420 --> 00:26:55,980
♪The time is right, even the wind is on our side♪

444
00:26:55,980 --> 00:26:59,340
♪At this very moment, the sun and moon shine on us♪

445
00:26:59,340 --> 00:27:01,340
♪Never mind what others may say♪

446
00:27:01,340 --> 00:27:02,940
♪Never mind how wild the rumours run♪

447
00:27:02,940 --> 00:27:06,060
♪I just happened to meet you, and that's all that matters♪

448
00:27:06,060 --> 00:27:09,220
♪The time is right, true love is on our side♪

449
00:27:09,760 --> 00:27:10,740
Knock it off.

450
00:27:12,470 --> 00:27:13,660
Just cooling you down.

451
00:27:14,700 --> 00:27:16,460
♪No need to pretend we're distant♪

452
00:27:16,460 --> 00:27:19,630
♪I just happened to meet you, and that's all that matters♪

453
00:27:19,630 --> 00:27:20,580
Thanks.

454
00:27:26,390 --> 00:27:29,020
How's the investigation into the knife attack going?

455
00:27:29,600 --> 00:27:30,980
We've pretty much figured it out.

456
00:27:31,760 --> 00:27:33,130
We know who he is now.

457
00:27:33,870 --> 00:27:36,500
He was one of my old boss's men when I was working undercover.

458
00:27:39,390 --> 00:27:40,770
He wants to avenge his boss.

459
00:27:41,280 --> 00:27:42,770
We're tracking him down now.

460
00:27:43,360 --> 00:27:44,130
Good.

461
00:27:44,840 --> 00:27:46,290
When you arrest him,

462
00:27:46,390 --> 00:27:48,130
make sure Officer Lam goes in first.

463
00:27:48,280 --> 00:27:49,420
He can take the hit for you.

464
00:27:49,870 --> 00:27:51,340
Don't joke about things like that.

465
00:27:51,360 --> 00:27:52,210
It's bad luck.

466
00:27:52,760 --> 00:27:53,740
Everything's fine

467
00:27:53,840 --> 00:27:54,820
until you say it.

468
00:27:55,040 --> 00:27:56,260
Are you saying someone might get hurt?

469
00:27:58,440 --> 00:27:59,210
It'll be fine.

470
00:28:00,200 --> 00:28:01,260
Don't worry.

471
00:28:04,390 --> 00:28:05,980
Doesn't sound like it'll be fine.

472
00:28:09,280 --> 00:28:10,340
Once we arrest him,

473
00:28:11,150 --> 00:28:14,130
my undercover assignment as Cheung Wai Keung will officially be over.

474
00:28:15,150 --> 00:28:17,530
Are you sure he doesn't have any other accomplices?

475
00:28:18,520 --> 00:28:19,370
What if he does?

476
00:28:19,550 --> 00:28:20,370
Then what?

477
00:28:23,470 --> 00:28:25,610
Since when do you know so much about gang business?

478
00:28:29,200 --> 00:28:30,740
Have you been

479
00:28:30,760 --> 00:28:32,370
doing all sorts of shady things

480
00:28:32,390 --> 00:28:33,450
and never telling me?

481
00:28:33,470 --> 00:28:35,050
It's just common sense.

482
00:28:35,760 --> 00:28:38,580
Gangsters rarely go alone on dangerous jobs.

483
00:28:38,600 --> 00:28:41,370
They usually move in groups of three or five.

484
00:28:41,600 --> 00:28:44,740
I'm a police officer. Situations like this come with the job.

485
00:28:44,790 --> 00:28:45,740
Even if it's dangerous,

486
00:28:45,760 --> 00:28:46,770
I still have to do my job.

487
00:28:52,360 --> 00:28:55,130
Why not come off the front line?

488
00:29:01,440 --> 00:29:02,290
What?

489
00:29:02,920 --> 00:29:04,530
You want me to back off whenever things get dangerous?

490
00:29:05,470 --> 00:29:08,370
Do you think I'm the type to run away?

491
00:29:08,600 --> 00:29:10,580
No, and that's exactly why I'm telling you this.

492
00:29:12,710 --> 00:29:14,530
I really don't think you should stay on frontline duty.

493
00:29:15,360 --> 00:29:16,370
Take a desk job.

494
00:29:16,950 --> 00:29:18,530
You can still do plenty of good there.

495
00:29:19,600 --> 00:29:21,770
You'd have a safe office with air conditioning,

496
00:29:21,920 --> 00:29:23,020
a clear career path,

497
00:29:23,360 --> 00:29:24,580
and no need to risk your life.

498
00:29:26,600 --> 00:29:27,980
It is safe.

499
00:29:28,550 --> 00:29:29,690
But it's not what I want.

500
00:29:31,200 --> 00:29:32,530
So being out in all weathers

501
00:29:32,950 --> 00:29:34,530
and risking your life is what you want?

502
00:29:37,680 --> 00:29:38,660
I'm not being stubborn.

503
00:29:39,680 --> 00:29:42,370
This is my choice.

504
00:29:43,870 --> 00:29:45,260
No matter how hard it gets,

505
00:29:45,520 --> 00:29:47,260
no matter what it costs me,

506
00:29:47,870 --> 00:29:50,500
I want to bring criminals to justice

507
00:29:51,790 --> 00:29:53,500
and help people in need.

508
00:29:54,200 --> 00:29:55,130
That's the reason

509
00:29:56,470 --> 00:29:57,930
I became a police officer in the first place.

510
00:30:07,680 --> 00:30:08,740
You didn't bring a lighter?

511
00:30:24,150 --> 00:30:25,050
I get it.

512
00:30:27,230 --> 00:30:28,450
But I just can't agree with you.

513
00:30:34,230 --> 00:30:36,610
If you overthink everything,

514
00:30:36,950 --> 00:30:38,770
you'll only end up lost and unsure.

515
00:30:42,760 --> 00:30:43,900
Do you remember

516
00:30:44,000 --> 00:30:46,500
the first film we ever watched together?

517
00:30:47,150 --> 00:30:48,610
Of course I do.

518
00:30:48,680 --> 00:30:51,020
You made me watch a romantic film for no reason.

519
00:30:51,150 --> 00:30:52,340
A romantic film?

520
00:30:52,470 --> 00:30:53,610
Which one was it?

521
00:30:54,680 --> 00:30:56,050
That one.

522
00:30:56,070 --> 00:30:57,020
I remember

523
00:30:57,040 --> 00:30:58,370
Leon Lai was in it.

524
00:30:58,520 --> 00:30:59,850
Who was the female lead?

525
00:31:00,000 --> 00:31:01,340
The female lead?

526
00:31:13,840 --> 00:31:15,820
Lai Siu Kwan and Lee Kiu

527
00:31:16,470 --> 00:31:18,340
spent all those years going round in circles.

528
00:31:19,150 --> 00:31:20,850
They clearly loved each other deeply,

529
00:31:22,120 --> 00:31:24,740
but reality kept holding them back,

530
00:31:25,630 --> 00:31:27,610
so they missed their chance time and again.

531
00:31:28,790 --> 00:31:29,660
Any thoughts?

532
00:31:30,150 --> 00:31:32,500
If they'd been truer to what they really wanted

533
00:31:32,920 --> 00:31:34,050
and worried less,

534
00:31:34,280 --> 00:31:37,020
would things have ended with fewer regrets?

535
00:31:37,760 --> 00:31:40,260
I don't think the problem was that they worried too much.

536
00:31:41,760 --> 00:31:43,690
It was that Lai Siu Kwan and Lee Kiu

537
00:31:43,840 --> 00:31:46,290
always thought there'd be another chance,

538
00:31:46,840 --> 00:31:48,290
that their feelings would never change.

539
00:31:49,150 --> 00:31:50,530
But they never considered

540
00:31:51,520 --> 00:31:52,740
that life changes,

541
00:31:52,760 --> 00:31:53,980
the world changes,

542
00:31:54,230 --> 00:31:56,260
and most of all, time passes.

543
00:31:58,550 --> 00:32:00,260
Sometimes, if you miss your chance with someone, that's it.

544
00:32:03,150 --> 00:32:04,500
The ending

545
00:32:04,760 --> 00:32:07,050
was only there so the audience

546
00:32:07,550 --> 00:32:08,660
wouldn't be left with any regrets.

547
00:32:09,360 --> 00:32:10,580
It doesn't really mean much.

548
00:32:12,280 --> 00:32:13,610
Then I disagree.

549
00:32:16,630 --> 00:32:18,420
What makes their relationship so moving

550
00:32:19,120 --> 00:32:21,610
is that they couldn't help loving each other despite everything.

551
00:32:22,840 --> 00:32:26,980
Most people are pushed along by circumstances.

552
00:32:27,470 --> 00:32:28,340
Not everyone is like you,

553
00:32:28,680 --> 00:32:30,450
able to keep everything firmly under control.

554
00:32:33,230 --> 00:32:34,660
But the way they cared about each other

555
00:32:34,840 --> 00:32:36,020
and the feelings they had for each other

556
00:32:36,280 --> 00:32:37,610
never changed

557
00:32:38,950 --> 00:32:39,980
from beginning to end.

558
00:32:42,280 --> 00:32:44,900
And I think a love that pure

559
00:32:45,760 --> 00:32:48,900
is far more precious than having no regrets.

560
00:32:49,950 --> 00:32:51,050
No matter how precious it is,

561
00:32:51,070 --> 00:32:53,260
nothing matters more than staying alive.

562
00:32:54,840 --> 00:32:57,580
I don't think anyone wants to miss their chance with the one they love.

563
00:32:59,040 --> 00:33:00,610
If you're not even alive anymore,

564
00:33:01,310 --> 00:33:02,660
no matter how deep the attachment

565
00:33:02,680 --> 00:33:04,050
or how sincere the feelings,

566
00:33:04,600 --> 00:33:05,370
it'll all come to nothing.

567
00:33:06,230 --> 00:33:07,930
Just think about that Mickey Mouse.

568
00:33:09,040 --> 00:33:11,660
But if you've got something like that Mickey Mouse tattoo

569
00:33:11,680 --> 00:33:13,020
that can make the one you love laugh and cry,

570
00:33:14,680 --> 00:33:16,340
then you've lived a life worth living.

571
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:30,450
That's why I say you've got no taste.

572
00:33:31,600 --> 00:33:33,690
That film portrays its characters' inner lives so delicately

573
00:33:33,710 --> 00:33:36,180
and weaves the period setting so skilfully

574
00:33:36,200 --> 00:33:38,020
into the characters' fates,

575
00:33:39,360 --> 00:33:40,660
and you say I forced you to watch it.

576
00:33:42,830 --> 00:33:45,710
[Private Property, No Entry]

577
00:33:57,550 --> 00:33:58,340
What are you doing?

578
00:33:59,040 --> 00:34:01,020
Trying to carve another Mickey Mouse?

579
00:34:02,070 --> 00:34:03,050
What is it, Officer?

580
00:34:03,200 --> 00:34:04,450
Going to charge me with vandalism?

581
00:34:04,840 --> 00:34:06,260
It depends on how good your drawing is.

582
00:34:12,470 --> 00:34:13,260
What is this?

583
00:34:13,870 --> 00:34:14,850
Our cigarette.

584
00:34:17,630 --> 00:34:18,580
Seriously, Mr. Hui?

585
00:34:19,470 --> 00:34:21,420
Your drawing skills need work.

586
00:34:22,440 --> 00:34:23,770
Give it to me.

587
00:34:53,920 --> 00:34:54,690
Much better.

588
00:35:05,150 --> 00:35:05,930
Hello?

589
00:35:09,280 --> 00:35:10,290
All right. I'm coming back now.

590
00:35:10,550 --> 00:35:11,820
Copy that. I'll be right there.

591
00:35:13,870 --> 00:35:15,290
- I've got a case to deal with.
- Something's come up at the office.

592
00:35:15,790 --> 00:35:16,420
Let's go.

593
00:35:18,120 --> 00:35:18,900
Get in.

594
00:35:24,710 --> 00:35:26,100
What you've been dealing with lately

595
00:35:26,390 --> 00:35:27,370
isn't against the law, is it?

596
00:35:28,950 --> 00:35:30,660
Someone was being ungrateful.

597
00:35:30,680 --> 00:35:31,900
I just taught him a lesson.

598
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:34,930
That's not illegal, is it, Officer?

599
00:35:35,870 --> 00:35:37,580
Just be careful.

600
00:35:39,200 --> 00:35:40,580
I should be saying that to you.

601
00:35:40,760 --> 00:35:42,020
Be careful.

602
00:35:55,650 --> 00:35:58,250
[Harbour Crystal Centre]

603
00:36:02,630 --> 00:36:03,420
Auntie Fan.

604
00:36:03,600 --> 00:36:04,820
Vincent.

605
00:36:04,870 --> 00:36:06,260
Why? Why did you do this?

606
00:36:06,280 --> 00:36:07,580
- Auntie Fan, calm down.
- Why? Why did you do this?

607
00:36:07,680 --> 00:36:08,450
Calm down?

608
00:36:08,470 --> 00:36:10,660
You need to explain this to me!

609
00:36:12,070 --> 00:36:13,450
The police found Uncle To's body.

610
00:36:13,840 --> 00:36:14,610
What happened?

611
00:36:14,790 --> 00:36:15,820
I need some time to find out.

612
00:36:16,470 --> 00:36:17,610
He was perfectly fine.

613
00:36:17,630 --> 00:36:19,290
After he came to see you here, he was killed.

614
00:36:19,310 --> 00:36:20,690
Tell me what happened.

615
00:36:21,040 --> 00:36:23,290
Auntie Fan, Uncle To did come to me.

616
00:36:23,310 --> 00:36:24,290
But I swear,

617
00:36:24,310 --> 00:36:25,850
I had nothing to do with his death.

618
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:26,900
Then why?

619
00:36:27,520 --> 00:36:28,980
Why did he die so miserably?

620
00:36:29,760 --> 00:36:32,290
Auntie Fan, calm down and think carefully.

621
00:36:32,600 --> 00:36:34,420
Who had Uncle To been seeing lately?

622
00:36:34,440 --> 00:36:36,770
Where had he been, and who had he contacted?

623
00:36:42,630 --> 00:36:43,990
[Police]

624
00:36:43,790 --> 00:36:45,050
Hong Kong, China Police!

625
00:36:45,280 --> 00:36:46,420
Everyone inside, listen up.

626
00:36:46,600 --> 00:36:48,850
We suspect someone on the premises is using counterfeit notes.

627
00:36:49,280 --> 00:36:51,290
We have a court-issued search warrant.

628
00:36:51,310 --> 00:36:52,420
Open the door immediately.

629
00:36:52,920 --> 00:36:54,450
Do not obstruct us in the course of our duties.

630
00:36:54,470 --> 00:36:56,210
If you refuse, we will force entry.

631
00:36:57,390 --> 00:36:58,180
Open the door!

632
00:37:00,470 --> 00:37:01,180
Boss,

633
00:37:01,200 --> 00:37:02,370
the police are outside.

634
00:37:06,440 --> 00:37:08,020
Auntie Fan, about Uncle To,

635
00:37:08,040 --> 00:37:09,610
we'll talk later. Wait here for me.

636
00:37:13,070 --> 00:37:14,900
Remember, as far as the public knows, you're the chairman of Tin Ping.

637
00:37:15,040 --> 00:37:17,690
If this blows up and Mrs. Hui hears about it, we're in trouble.

638
00:37:17,840 --> 00:37:18,530
Got it.

639
00:37:22,550 --> 00:37:23,260
Turn on the lights.

640
00:37:23,280 --> 00:37:24,370
Routine police check.

641
00:37:24,920 --> 00:37:26,420
Everyone, get up and stand to the side.

642
00:37:26,760 --> 00:37:27,930
Show your IDs.

643
00:37:28,440 --> 00:37:29,450
Move it.

644
00:37:32,630 --> 00:37:33,420
Officers,

645
00:37:34,360 --> 00:37:35,660
how can I assist you?

646
00:37:36,470 --> 00:37:37,980
We're with the Commercial Crime Bureau.

647
00:37:38,710 --> 00:37:39,580
Are you in charge here?

648
00:37:40,200 --> 00:37:40,930
I am.

649
00:37:41,600 --> 00:37:42,370
Here's the search warrant.

650
00:37:43,120 --> 00:37:45,180
We suspect someone here of using and possessing

651
00:37:45,200 --> 00:37:46,420
counterfeit notes.

652
00:37:47,230 --> 00:37:47,820
Go.

653
00:37:48,040 --> 00:37:48,850
Take him in.

654
00:37:51,520 --> 00:37:52,260
Mr. Hui,

655
00:37:52,520 --> 00:37:54,450
please come with us to the station to assist with our investigation.

656
00:37:55,630 --> 00:37:57,100
Need a hood?

657
00:37:57,920 --> 00:37:59,020
This is my turf.

658
00:37:59,520 --> 00:38:00,770
I've got nothing to fear.

659
00:38:04,070 --> 00:38:04,850
Look out!

660
00:38:06,790 --> 00:38:08,020
You traitor!

661
00:38:21,280 --> 00:38:22,660
Joseph, call an ambulance.

662
00:38:22,870 --> 00:38:23,580
Yes, sir.

663
00:38:24,520 --> 00:38:26,610
Shots fired. Someone's been hit. Send an ambulance.

664
00:38:33,360 --> 00:38:34,130
Are you all right?

665
00:38:35,840 --> 00:38:37,500
Take everyone back to the station. We'll deal with it there!

666
00:38:42,200 --> 00:38:43,290
Come back to the station with me.

667
00:38:51,660 --> 00:38:56,700
[Episode 3]

668
00:38:56,790 --> 00:39:11,990
[This story is fictional. Any resemblance is entirely coincidental.]

